% ; is a regular (higher-order) predicate in Elpi, defined by exactly two
% rules -- so a ! written inside one of its disjuncts only cuts back to
% that rule selection, one stack frame up: it discards ;'s own untried
% alternative, but does not reach further out to cut p's own second rule.
% In Teyjus and standard lambda-Prolog, where ; is a built-in control
% construct and the cut is transparent through it, p's second rule would
% be cut away too.

pred p.
p :- (!, fail ; true).
p :- print "p's second rule fired".

main :- p, print "after p".
